  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "PREOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS & PROCEDURE",
      "text": "The patient underwent uncomplicated laparoscopic cholecystectomy for symptomatic cholelithiasis under general endotracheal anesthesia."
    },
    {
      "title": "HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS",
      "text": "The patient is an adult who presented electively for surgical intervention following conservative management failure. Pre-admission testing confirmed that preoperative bun was 14.3 mg/dL. Preoperative metabolic screening showed a baseline potassium of 4.12 mmol/L. The patient was cleared from a cardiopulmonary standpoint and taken to the operative suite."
    },
    {
      "title": "POSTOPERATIVE HOSPITAL COURSE",
      "text": "The patient was extubated in the operating room and transferred to the post-anesthesia care unit in stable condition. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. For pain and infection prophylaxis, the patient was prescribed Amlodipine 5 mg PO every morning. On postoperative day one, postoperative white blood cell count remained stable at 7.1 10*3/uL. Surgical incisions were clean, intact, and without erythema or purulent drainage."
    },
    {
      "title": "POST-DISCHARGE MEDICATIONS",
      "text": "Discharge medications: The patient will take Cephalexin 500 mg orally QID for 10 days, and continue baseline Amoxicillin 250 mg PO TID for 7 days. All prescriptions were transmitted electronically to the patient's pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "title": "ACTIVITY & WOUND CARE PLAN",
      "text": "Keep dressing clean and dry. No heavy lifting greater than 10 pounds for two weeks. Surgical clinic follow-up scheduled in 10 days."
    }
  ],
